Solve:
\[
2 \log _{4} x-\log _{4}(x+3)=1
\]

\section*{Solution}
\[
\begin{aligned}
2 \log _{4} x-\log _{4}(x+3) & =1 \\
\log _{4}\left(\frac{x^{2}}{x+3}\right) & =1 \\
4^{1} & =\frac{x^{2}}{x+3} \\
4 x+12 & =x^{2} \\
x^{2}-4 x-12 & =0 \\
(x-6)(x+2) & =0 \\
x=6 \quad x>-2 &
\end{aligned}
\]

